cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  HCS-proc: data processing pipeline for High-Content Screening
  using CellProfiler data
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  article listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
abstract: >-
  HCS-proc is the image analysis and data processing pipeline behind a
  high-content screen of RTgill-W1 fish gill cells exposed to
  Tebuthiuron, published in Tome et al. 2026. It runs from raw
  microscopy images to the reduced feature space the article's
  conclusions rest on: image-level quality control by
  CellProfiler-Analyst classifiers under Nextflow, CellProfiler
  feature extraction and per-cell pooling, row and plate
  standardization with percentile trimming, concentration-response
  feature selection by earth mover's distance (EMD) and multi-model
  curve fitting, feature categorization, and dimensionality reduction
  by UMAP alongside MMD, EMD and Mahalanobis distance measures. Each
  step is a script driven by an .ini configuration file, and the
  README documents the sequence they must run in. Release v1
  (10.5281/zenodo.17949848) is the exact code used for the article;
  later releases carry corrections and extensions. The
  concentration-response feature selection has since been generalised
  into the standalone tool cdr_FS (10.5281/zenodo.22047439).
